  "description": "Learn how to talk about your body parts, symptoms, and visits to the doctor in Chinese.",
  "guidebook": "### Expressing Aches and Pains\nIn Chinese, expressing pain is straightforward. You typically use a topic-comment structure: **Person + Body Part + 疼 (téng)**.\n- **我头疼。** (*Wǒ tóu téng.*) — My head hurts.\n- **他的手疼。** (*Tā de shǒu téng.*) — His hand hurts.\n\n### Describing Sickness\nWhen you feel under the weather, use **不舒服** (*bù shūfu* - not comfortable/unwell):\n- **我有点不舒服。** (*Wǒ yǒudiǎn bù shūfu.*) — I feel a bit unwell.\n\n### Taking Medicine\nIn English, you \"take\" medicine, but in Chinese, you \"eat\" it using the verb **吃** (*chī*):\n- **吃药** (*chī yào*) — to take medicine.",
